------- FILE main.asm
------- FILE wander.asm LEVEL 2 PASS 3
      0  7029					      include	"wander.asm"
      1  7029							; Fat Chip 64 - chord changes, DRONE and One Key Play (v0.27)
      2  7029							;
      3  7029							; CHORD CHANGE (PLAYING): how the voices move when the chord changes.
      4  7029							;   AS MODE  DRONE wanders, the other modes ATTACK
      5  7029							;   ATTACK   as always: the new notes start
      6  7029							;   GLIDE    every voice slides to its new note (a glide even if the patch
      7  7029							;	      has none)
      8  7029							;   STAGGER  the SID and the bass voices glide, the Game Boy and NES pulses
      9  7029							;	      start again
     10  7029							;   WANDER   each voice moves at its own moment within WANDER TIME, the bass
     11  7029							;	      late; some glide, some start again (fade out, come back in)
     12  7029							; DRONE (C= + Z): the lowest key held is the root: open fifths up from it
     13  7029							;   (DRONE VOICING: FIFTHS, FIFTHS + 9TH, SUS4). A new key moves the drone.
     14  7029							; ONE KEY PLAY: the cursor keys step through a phrase (pentatonic pairs or
     15  7029							;   the chord's notes); alternate the two for fast runs. See OkpPress.
     16  7029
